"Integrating embedded hardware and physical computing solutions."

[ C. Right Column: Asset Placeholder ]

Positioning: Absolute positioning on the right side. Spans from 70vw to 90vw horizontally, and 30vh to 75vh vertically.

Visual: Currently a dashed border placeholder. It will eventually hold an interactive WebGL or media asset representing the technical themes.

MICRO-INTERACTION 1: THE HEAT HAZE (Text Stabilization)
(Mechanics remain standard as per earlier specification when text interactions are built).

The biography text is highly volatile and difficult to read until the user
intervenes with their cursor.

Default State (Volatile):

The text is wrapped in individual <span> tags per word.

CSS: color: transparent; text-shadow: 0 0 12px rgba(248, 250, 252, 0.6);

Effect: The text looks like a glowing, blurry heat haze.

Hover State (The Cooling Stabilizer):

The mouse event listener calculates distance between the cursor and each word.

Radius: 150px around the cursor.

Action: Any <span> within that radius gets a .cooled class.

.cooled CSS: color: #F8FAFC; text-shadow: 0 0 0px rgba(248,250,252,1);

Transition: transition: all 0.2s ease-out;

UX Result: As the user sweeps the mouse over the text, the blur instantly
snaps into crisp, readable text, leaving a fading trail of blur behind it.

MICRO-INTERACTION 2: THE PLASMA SHOOTER (Border Melting)

The user can "shoot" the structural UI boxes on the left to interact with the environment.

Cursor Override:

As soon as the user enters the About section, the cursor changes to a
custom SVG reticle. cursor: url('/assets/plasma-reticle.svg') 16 16, crosshair;

Click Event (The Shot):

When the user clicks on one of the Tech Stack UI boxes, it triggers a
temporary "Melt" state for that specific box.

The Melt State (Active):

Duration: 1.5 seconds.

Border Distortion: Uses an inline SVG filter <feDisplacementMap> mapped
to the border, OR rapid CSS border-radius manipulation (e.g., changing
from 4px to 40% 60% 70% 30% randomly).

Glow Injection: box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(249, 115, 22, 0.8); (Bright plasma orange).

Border Color: Shifts from #1E293B to #F97316.

The Healing State (Recovery):

After 1.5 seconds, the SVG filter is removed, and the CSS properties
transition: all 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.25, 1, 0.5, 1); smoothly snap the
box back to its strict, rigid, default geometric shape.

TECHNICAL UX & PERFORMANCE NOTES

To prevent DOM thrashing with the Heat Haze effect, do NOT use React state
to track the mouse coordinates for the word spans. Use a useRef to hold
the container, and a single requestAnimationFrame loop in a useEffect
to toggle the .cooled classes directly on the DOM nodes.

The SVG Displacement filter for the melting boxes should be pre-defined in
the HTML <defs> tag and only applied via CSS class (filter: url(#melt))
on click, rather than generating the SVG dynamically on every click.